###
post: The whole program as a graph, drawn by Viv
agent: claude

`draw_program(g, title)` draws a `ProgramGraph` (lib/proggraph.viv) with the
figure records of a diagram: every def
that matters to the run as a box, the steps inside it as boxes in the order
they run, the loops that hold steps as dashed boxes around them, the calls
between defs as arrows from the step that makes each call, and the values
steps hand each other as arrows labeled with the variables. A value that
reaches the next pass of a loop is a dashed arrow back up.

Which defs are drawn: `<main>`, every def with steps that the run can reach,
and every def on a call path from `<main>` to one of them. When no def has
steps, every def the run reaches (up to `MAX_PLAIN_DEFS`). The defs these call
and that are not drawn are named at the foot of their caller's box.

The layout is `lib/graphlayout.viv`, twice: inside each box its children,
top to bottom; then the boxes of the defs, left to right, callers before
callees. Each box's id is its node's id (`hf_scf`, `hf_scf/fock`), so a page
can find the box of the def or step a reader is at.

`draw_view(g, v, title)` draws what a `GraphView` says: which defs are boxes,
how many callees each one hides (written `+3` at the right of its header, for
a page to open) or whether its callees are open (`−`), how many times each
call ran (written on its arrow when more than once), and where the boxes of an
earlier drawing were, so a redrawing after a box is opened moves the others as
little as it can. `draw_program` is `draw_view` with the defs chosen above and
nothing hidden, counted or remembered.

Every mark has an id a page can act on: a box is its node's id; an arrow is
`call:<step or def>-><def>`, `data:<step>-><step>`, `next:<step>-><step>` (a
value for the next pass) or `then:<step>-><step>` (the order of two steps);
the text of a node is `<id>#head`, `#text`, `#reads`, `#foot`, its marks
`#more` and `#less`; an arrow's text is `<arrow id>#vars` or `#count`. The
figure's x label says which way the defs run, `across` or `down`, so a page
that asks for a redrawing can keep it.

`draw_view_mp(g, v, mp, title)` also draws a program's multi-paths:
a stage with several implementations of one
intent, cross-checked against each other. Open, a multi-path is a fork (a
diamond named after the stage), one path per implementation, and a join (a
diamond with the agreement they are held to); the call into the fork carries
the stage's intent, the default's path is solid and the others are dashed.
Closed, it is one box, `multi-path ×n`, with the intent, the contract and how
many implementations are independent and were seen agreeing. An
implementation that is a drawn function is its own box on its path. The
marks: the closed box is `mp:<stage>@<host>`; open, `mp:<stage>@<host>/fork`,
`/join`, `/m:<name>`, and the arrows `mp:<stage>@<host>/in`, `/to:<name>`,
`/from:<name>`.

Used with `import graphdraw`.
###
from proggraph import node_index, ProgramGraph, reachable
from graphlayout import layered, layout_input, LayoutInput

#| Text sizes, in the drawing's units (a unit is a pixel at full size), and
#| the width of a character as a fraction of the size: the renderers use
#| these sizes, and a monospace character is 0.6 of its size in every font
#| they name. Sans text is estimated.
FONT_SMALL = 11
FONT_NORMAL = 13
FONT_LARGE = 15
MONO_EM = 0.6
SANS_EM = 0.56
#| Space inside a box, around its text and its children.
PAD = 8
#| Space between two lines of text.
LINE_GAP = 3
#| A step's box: least and greatest width.
STEP_MIN_W = 96
STEP_MAX_W = 220
#| A def's or loop's header: the widest it is written.
HEADER_MAX_W = 360
#| The longest variable list written on a value's arrow, in characters.
LABEL_MAX_CHARS = 26
#| Inside a box: space between children, and between ranks.
INNER_NODE_GAP = 22
INNER_RANK_GAP = 6
#| Between the boxes of the defs.
OUTER_NODE_GAP = 34
OUTER_RANK_GAP = 70
#| How much the order of the steps wants to be a straight line.
SEQUENCE_WEIGHT = 8
#| How much of a child's width the arcs meeting it spread over.
PORT_SPREAD = 0.7
#| The most arcs (values that skip a child, or go to the next pass) a box draws.
MAX_ARCS = 5
#| With no steps anywhere: at most this many defs.
MAX_PLAIN_DEFS = 40
#| Left to right unless the drawing would be more than this many times as
#| wide as tall; then top to bottom.
WIDE_RATIO = 2
#| The legend's height, above the drawing.
LEGEND_H = 30
#| Top to bottom, the space between the lanes that take a step's calls down
#| the right side of its def's box.
LANE_GAP = 7
#| Space between a node's header and its `+3` or `−` mark.
MARK_GAP = 10

#| What `draw_view` draws of a graph.
#: shown     per node: 1 for a def drawn as a box (its steps and loops come with it)
#: open      per node: 1 for a def whose callees are shown; its header ends in `−`
#: more      per node: how many callees of the def are not shown; its header ends in `+n`
#: counts    per edge: how many times the call ran; 0 when not known
#: hint_ids  the def boxes of an earlier drawing
#: hint_x    the left side of each, in that drawing
#: hint_y    its top, measured down from the drawing's top
#: dir       0 to choose, 1 for callees to the right of callers, 2 for below them
record GraphView {
    shown: Arr
    open: Arr
    more: Arr
    counts: Arr
    hint_ids: [Str]
    hint_x: Arr
    hint_y: Arr
    dir: Num
}

#| The multi-paths a drawing shows, one entry per stage and the def it hangs
#| from.
#: ids         the stage's id: `eri`
#: titles      its intent, in a line
#: contracts   what the members must agree on: `within 1e-12`
#: notes       how many members are independent and were seen agreeing
#: hosts       per entry: the node (a def) the fork hangs from
#: host_steps  the node of the step of it that makes the call; -1 for the def's header
#: members     the members' names, separated by spaces
#: defaults    the member the production path runs
#: ran         the members that ran, separated by spaces
#: open        1 for the fork, a path per member and the join; 0 for one box
record MultiPaths {
    ids: [Str]
    titles: [Str]
    contracts: [Str]
    notes: [Str]
    hosts: Arr
    host_steps: Arr
    members: [Str]
    defaults: [Str]
    ran: [Str]
    open: Arr
}

#| No multi-paths.
#@ a2fbd5be
def no_multipaths() -> MultiPaths {
    return MultiPaths { ids: split(""), titles: split(""), contracts: split(""), notes: split(""), hosts: zeros(0), host_steps: zeros(0), members: split(""), defaults: split(""), ran: split(""), open: zeros(0) }
}

#| A diamond's width around a label whose widest line is `tw` wide.
#@ a2b689c3
def diamond_w(tw) {
    return 2 * (tw + PAD)
}

#| A diamond's height around a label of `lines` lines.
#@ c0d47cf6
def diamond_h(lines) {
    return 2 * (lines * FONT_SMALL + (lines - 1) * LINE_GAP + PAD)
}

#| The view `draw_program` draws: the chosen defs, nothing hidden, counted or remembered.
def default_view(g: ProgramGraph) -> GraphView {
    n = len(g.ids)
    ne = len(g.edge_kinds)
    return GraphView { shown: chosen_defs(g), open: zeros(n), more: zeros(n), counts: zeros(ne), hint_ids: split(""), hint_x: zeros(0), hint_y: zeros(0), dir: 0 }
}

#| A whole number written with a comma between each three digits.
def grouped(v) -> Str {
    s = f"{floor(v):.0f}"
    out = ""
    k = len(s)
    while k > 3 {
        out = "," + s[k - 3:k] + out
        k -= 3
    }
    return s[:k] + out
}

#| The width of `s` at `size`, in monospace (`mono` 1) or sans.
def text_w(s: Str, size, mono) {
    em = SANS_EM
    if mono == 1 {
        em = MONO_EM
    }
    return len(s) * size * em
}

#| `s` cut to fit `maxw`, with an ellipsis when cut.
def fit(s: Str, maxw, size, mono) -> Str {
    if text_w(s, size, mono) <= maxw {
        return s
    }
    em = SANS_EM
    if mono == 1 {
        em = MONO_EM
    }
    keep = floor(maxw / (size * em)) - 1
    if keep < 1 {
        return "…"
    }
    return s[:keep] + "…"
}

#| Text safe for a figure record: no newline, no ` ; `.
def clean(s: Str) -> Str {
    return replace(replace(s, "\n", " "), " ; ", "; ")
}

#| A space-separated list of names written with commas, cut to `LABEL_MAX_CHARS`.
def names_label(vars: Str) -> Str {
    s = join(", ", split(vars))
    if len(s) > LABEL_MAX_CHARS {
        s = s[:LABEL_MAX_CHARS - 1] + "…"
    }
    return s
}

#| Which defs to draw: 1 for each, 0 for the rest (see the module's text).
def chosen_defs(g: ProgramGraph) -> Arr {
    n = len(g.ids)
    reach = reachable(g)
    main = node_index(g, "<main>")
    # a def with steps, and every def that calls toward one
    leads = zeros(n)
    for k to n {
        if g.kinds[k] == "step" and reach[k] == 1 {
            leads[g.owners[k]] = 1
        }
    }
    grew = true
    while grew {
        grew = false
        for e to len(g.edge_kinds) {
            if g.edge_kinds[e] == "call" {
                caller = g.owners[g.edge_from[e]]
                if leads[g.edge_to[e]] == 1 and leads[caller] == 0 and reach[caller] == 1 {
                    leads[caller] = 1
                    grew = true
                }
            }
        }
    }
    if main >= 0 {
        leads[main] = 1
    }
    if sum(leads) > 1 or main < 0 {
        return leads
    }
    # no steps: the defs the run reaches, nearest first
    chosen = zeros(n)
    chosen[main] = 1
    frontier = [main]
    count = 1
    while len(frontier) > 0 and count < MAX_PLAIN_DEFS {
        nextf = []
        for e to len(g.edge_kinds) {
            if g.edge_kinds[e] == "call" and count < MAX_PLAIN_DEFS {
                caller = g.owners[g.edge_from[e]]
                callee = g.edge_to[e]
                if chosen[callee] == 0 and has(frontier, caller) {
                    chosen[callee] = 1
                    nextf = append(nextf, callee)
                    count += 1
                }
            }
        }
        frontier = nextf
    }
    return chosen
}

#| Whether the number `v` is an element of `a`.
def has(a: Arr, v) {
    for x in a {
        if x == v {
            return true
        }
    }
    return false
}

#| The layout of the def boxes. Left to right (`down` false), across the
#| ranks is down the page and a call leaves its caller's side at the step that
#| makes it; top to bottom, a def's box is widened on the right by its lanes,
#| and a call leaves down its lane. A def of the view's earlier drawing is
#| hinted to stay where its box was.
def outer_input(oids: [Str], v: GraphView, defs: Arr, bw: Arr, bh: Arr, head_h: Arr, cfrom: Arr, cto: Arr, cport: Arr, cstep: Arr, clab: [Str], celen: Arr, clane: Arr, nlanes: Arr, down) -> LayoutInput {
    nd = len(defs)
    nc = len(cfrom)
    w = zeros(nd)
    h = zeros(nd)
    lw = zeros(nd)
    for i to nd {
        d = defs[i]
        if down {
            lw[i] = nlanes[i] * LANE_GAP
            w[i] = bw[d] + lw[i]
            h[i] = bh[d]
        }
        else {
            w[i] = bh[d]
            h[i] = bw[d]
        }
    }
    sport = zeros(nc)
    tport = zeros(nc)
    label_w = zeros(nc)
    label_h = zeros(nc)
    for q to nc {
        a = defs[cfrom[q]]
        b = defs[cto[q]]
        if down {
            sport[q] = -lw[cfrom[q]] / 2
            if cstep[q] >= 0 {
                sport[q] = (bw[a] - lw[cfrom[q]]) / 2 + LANE_GAP * (clane[q] + 1)
            }
            tport[q] = -lw[cto[q]] / 2
        }
        else {
            sport[q] = cport[q]
            tport[q] = head_h[b] / 2 - bh[b] / 2
        }
        if len(clab[q]) > 0 {
            tw = text_w(clab[q], FONT_SMALL, 1)
            if down {
                label_w[q] = tw
                label_h[q] = FONT_SMALL + LINE_GAP
            }
            else {
                label_w[q] = FONT_SMALL + LINE_GAP
                label_h[q] = tw + 2 * LINE_GAP
            }
        }
    }
    hint = zeros(nd)
    hinted = zeros(nd)
    for i to nd {
        id = oids[i]
        if id in v.hint_ids {
            j = index(v.hint_ids, id)
            hinted[i] = 1
            if down {
                hint[i] = v.hint_x[j] + w[i] / 2
            }
            else {
                hint[i] = v.hint_y[j] - LEGEND_H + bh[defs[i]] / 2
            }
        }
    }
    inp = layout_input(w, h, cfrom, cto, OUTER_NODE_GAP, OUTER_RANK_GAP)
    return LayoutInput { sport: sport, tport: tport, label_w: label_w, label_h: label_h, elen: celen, hint: hint, hinted: hinted, sides: 0, ..inp }
}

#| The drawing: every box, arrow and text of the graph `g`, as figure records.
def draw_program(g: ProgramGraph, title: Str) {
    return draw_view(g, default_view(g), title)
}

#| The drawing of what `view` shows of `g` (see the module's text).
def draw_view(g: ProgramGraph, view: GraphView, title: Str) {
    return draw_view_mp(g, view, no_multipaths(), title)
}

#| `draw_view`, with the multi-paths `mp` drawn where they hang.
#@ 1ed48679
def draw_view_mp(g: ProgramGraph, view: GraphView, mp: MultiPaths, title: Str) {
    n = len(g.ids)
    chosen = view.shown
    # ---- the drawn nodes: the chosen defs and the steps and loops inside them
    dmap = zeros(n) - 1
    gi = []
    for k to n {
        keep = false
        if g.kinds[k] == "def" {
            keep = chosen[k] == 1
        }
        else if g.kinds[k] == "step" or g.kinds[k] == "loop" {
            keep = chosen[g.owners[k]] == 1
        }
        if keep {
            dmap[k] = len(gi)
            gi = append(gi, k)
        }
    }
    m = len(gi)
    par = zeros(m) - 1
    for d to m {
        p = g.parents[gi[d]]
        if p >= 0 {
            par[d] = dmap[p]
        }
    }
    depth = zeros(m)
    changed = true
    while changed {
        changed = false
        for d to m {
            if par[d] >= 0 and depth[d] != depth[par[d]] + 1 {
                depth[d] = depth[par[d]] + 1
                changed = true
            }
        }
    }
    maxdepth = 0
    if m > 0 {
        maxdepth = max(depth)
    }
    nkids = zeros(m)
    for d to m {
        if par[d] >= 0 {
            nkids[par[d]] += 1
        }
    }

    # ---- what each def calls that is not drawn: the foot of its box
    calls_out = []
    for d to m {
        k = gi[d]
        others = split("")
        for e to len(g.edge_kinds) {
            if g.edge_kinds[e] == "call" and g.owners[g.edge_from[e]] == k {
                name = g.labels[g.edge_to[e]]
                if chosen[g.edge_to[e]] == 0 and name not in others {
                    others = append(others, name)
                }
            }
        }
        text = ""
        if g.kinds[k] == "def" and len(others) > 0 {
            text = "calls " + join(", ", others)
        }
        calls_out = append(calls_out, text)
    }

    # ---- the values steps hand each other, at the box that holds both ends
    de_lca = []
    de_from = []
    de_to = []
    de_vars = []
    de_back = []
    for e to len(g.edge_kinds) {
        if g.edge_kinds[e] != "data" {
            continue
        }
        s = dmap[g.edge_from[e]]
        t = dmap[g.edge_to[e]]
        if s < 0 or t < 0 {
            continue
        }
        # climb from the deeper end until the two share a parent
        a = s
        b = t
        while depth[a] > depth[b] {
            a = par[a]
        }
        while depth[b] > depth[a] {
            b = par[b]
        }
        while par[a] != par[b] {
            a = par[a]
            b = par[b]
        }
        if a == b {
            continue
        }
        de_lca = append(de_lca, par[a])
        de_from = append(de_from, a)
        de_to = append(de_to, b)
        de_vars = append(de_vars, g.edge_vars[e])
        de_back = append(de_back, g.edge_carried[e])
    }
    nde = len(de_lca)

    # ---- which values are drawn as arrows. Between a child and the next one
    # the arrow is short and always drawn; one that skips children, or goes
    # back to an earlier pass, is an arc around them, and a box draws at most
    # MAX_ARCS arcs (values for the next pass first). The values of the arcs
    # it leaves out are written in the box they reach, as "reads ...".
    place = zeros(m)
    seen_kids = zeros(m)
    for d to m {
        if par[d] >= 0 {
            place[d] = seen_kids[par[d]]
            seen_kids[par[d]] += 1
        }
    }
    de_keep = zeros(nde) + 1
    for d to m {
        # the arcs of this box, as distinct (from, to, back), carried ones first
        arc_from = []
        arc_to = []
        arc_back = []
        for pass to 2 {
            want_back = 1 - pass
            for j to nde {
                if de_lca[j] != d or de_back[j] != want_back {
                    continue
                }
                if de_back[j] == 0 and place[de_to[j]] == place[de_from[j]] + 1 {
                    continue
                }
                known = false
                for q to len(arc_from) {
                    if arc_from[q] == de_from[j] and arc_to[q] == de_to[j] and arc_back[q] == de_back[j] {
                        known = true
                    }
                }
                if not known {
                    arc_from = append(arc_from, de_from[j])
                    arc_to = append(arc_to, de_to[j])
                    arc_back = append(arc_back, de_back[j])
                }
            }
        }
        for q from MAX_ARCS to len(arc_from) {
            for j to nde {
                if de_from[j] == arc_from[q] and de_to[j] == arc_to[q] and de_back[j] == arc_back[q] {
                    de_keep[j] = 0
                }
            }
        }
    }
    # a value that skips a box of steps (a loop, a step with steps inside)
    # would run down beside it, far from both ends: it is not drawn, and its
    # variables are written in the step it reaches
    for j to nde {
        if de_back[j] == 1 or de_keep[j] == 0 {
            continue
        }
        for c to m {
            if par[c] == de_lca[j] and nkids[c] > 0 and place[c] > place[de_from[j]] and place[c] < place[de_to[j]] {
                de_keep[j] = 0
            }
        }
    }
    # what each box reads from arcs not drawn
    far = []
    for d to m {
        vars = split("")
        for j to nde {
            if de_keep[j] == 0 and de_to[j] == d {
                for v in split(de_vars[j]) {
                    if v not in vars {
                        vars = append(vars, v)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        text = ""
        if len(vars) > 0 {
            text = "reads " + join(", ", vars)
        }
        far = append(far, text)
    }

    # ---- a def's mark: `+n` when it hides callees, `−` when they are open
    marks = []
    for d to m {
        k = gi[d]
        mk = ""
        if g.kinds[k] == "def" and view.more[k] > 0 {
            mk = "+" + grouped(view.more[k])
        }
        else if g.kinds[k] == "def" and view.open[k] == 1 {
            mk = "−"
        }
        marks = append(marks, mk)
    }

    # ---- sizes, deepest boxes first; children placed inside their parent
    bw = zeros(m)
    bh = zeros(m)
    head_h = zeros(m)
    relx = zeros(m)
    rely = zeros(m)
    cox = zeros(m)
    coy = zeros(m)
    # the text of each box: its header, a step's text, a def's foot
    head = []
    sub = []
    ins = []
    foot = []
    hw = zeros(m)
    hh = zeros(m)
    fw = zeros(m)
    fh = zeros(m)
    for d to m {
        k = gi[d]
        kind = g.kinds[k]
        h1 = clean(g.labels[k])
        h2 = ""
        if kind == "def" {
            h1 = clean(fit(g.labels[k] + "(" + join(", ", split(g.params[k])) + ")", HEADER_MAX_W, FONT_NORMAL, 1))
        }
        else if kind == "loop" {
            h1 = clean(fit(g.labels[k], HEADER_MAX_W, FONT_SMALL, 1))
        }
        else {
            h2 = clean(fit(g.texts[k], STEP_MAX_W - 2 * PAD, FONT_SMALL, 0))
        }
        hw[d] = text_w(h1, FONT_NORMAL, 1)
        if kind == "def" and len(marks[d]) > 0 {
            hw[d] += MARK_GAP + text_w(marks[d], FONT_SMALL, 1)
        }
        hh[d] = FONT_NORMAL + 2 * PAD
        if kind == "loop" {
            hw[d] = text_w(h1, FONT_SMALL, 1)
            hh[d] = FONT_SMALL + 2 * PAD
        }
        h3 = ""
        if kind == "step" and len(far[d]) > 0 {
            h3 = clean(fit(far[d], STEP_MAX_W - 2 * PAD, FONT_SMALL, 1))
        }
        lines_below = 0
        if len(h2) > 0 {
            hw[d] = max(hw[d], text_w(h2, FONT_SMALL, 0))
            lines_below += 1
        }
        if len(h3) > 0 {
            hw[d] = max(hw[d], text_w(h3, FONT_SMALL, 1))
            lines_below += 1
        }
        hh[d] = hh[d] + lines_below * (FONT_SMALL + LINE_GAP)
        f1 = ""
        if len(calls_out[d]) > 0 {
            f1 = clean(fit(calls_out[d], max(hw[d], STEP_MAX_W), FONT_SMALL, 0))
            fw[d] = text_w(f1, FONT_SMALL, 0)
            fh[d] = FONT_SMALL + PAD
        }
        head = append(head, h1)
        sub = append(sub, h2)
        ins = append(ins, h3)
        foot = append(foot, f1)
    }
    # routes inside boxes, relative to the box's children's origin
    r_owner = []
    r_start = []
    r_x = []
    r_y = []
    r_style = []
    r_id = []
    r_label = []
    r_lx = []
    r_ly = []
    for level from maxdepth to -1 by -1 {
        for d to m {
            if depth[d] != level {
                continue
            }
            k = gi[d]
            head_h[d] = hh[d]
            if nkids[d] == 0 {
                bw[d] = max(hw[d], fw[d]) + 2 * PAD
                if g.kinds[k] == "step" {
                    bw[d] = min(STEP_MAX_W, max(STEP_MIN_W, bw[d]))
                }
                bh[d] = hh[d] + fh[d]
                continue
            }
            # the children, top to bottom in the order they run
            kids = []
            for c to m {
                if par[c] == d {
                    kids = append(kids, c)
                }
            }
            nk = len(kids)
            local = zeros(m) - 1
            kw = zeros(nk)
            kh = zeros(nk)
            for i to nk {
                local[kids[i]] = i
                kw[i] = bw[kids[i]]
                kh[i] = bh[kids[i]]
            }
            efrom = []
            eto = []
            eback = []
            ew = []
            evars = []
            estyle = []
            eid = []
            # a value between two children, merged with others between the same two
            for j to len(de_lca) {
                if de_lca[j] != d or de_keep[j] == 0 {
                    continue
                }
                a = local[de_from[j]]
                b = local[de_to[j]]
                found = -1
                for q to len(efrom) {
                    if efrom[q] == a and eto[q] == b and eback[q] == de_back[j] {
                        found = q
                    }
                }
                if found >= 0 {
                    merged = evars[found]
                    for v in split(de_vars[j]) {
                        if v not in split(merged) {
                            merged = merged + " " + v
                        }
                    }
                    evars = evars[:found] + [merged] + evars[found + 1:]
                    continue
                }
                efrom = append(efrom, a)
                eto = append(eto, b)
                eback = append(eback, de_back[j])
                ew = append(ew, 1)
                evars = append(evars, de_vars[j])
                if de_back[j] == 1 {
                    estyle = append(estyle, "s2 dash curved")
                    eid = append(eid, "next:" + g.ids[gi[de_from[j]]] + "->" + g.ids[gi[de_to[j]]])
                }
                else {
                    estyle = append(estyle, "s5 curved")
                    eid = append(eid, "data:" + g.ids[gi[de_from[j]]] + "->" + g.ids[gi[de_to[j]]])
                }
            }
            # the order they run in: from each child to the next, straight
            for i from 1 to nk {
                found = -1
                for q to len(efrom) {
                    if efrom[q] == i - 1 and eto[q] == i and eback[q] == 0 {
                        found = q
                    }
                }
                if found >= 0 {
                    ew[found] = SEQUENCE_WEIGHT
                }
                else {
                    efrom = append(efrom, i - 1)
                    eto = append(eto, i)
                    eback = append(eback, 0)
                    ew = append(ew, SEQUENCE_WEIGHT)
                    evars = append(evars, "")
                    estyle = append(estyle, "muted thin")
                    eid = append(eid, "then:" + g.ids[gi[kids[i - 1]]] + "->" + g.ids[gi[kids[i]]])
                }
            }
            # arcs that meet at one child are spread along its side, not piled on its middle
            ne_here = len(efrom)
            sp = zeros(ne_here)
            tp = zeros(ne_here)
            for i to nk {
                for end to 2 {
                    count = 0
                    for q to ne_here {
                        if ew[q] != SEQUENCE_WEIGHT and ((end == 0 and efrom[q] == i) or (end == 1 and eto[q] == i)) {
                            count += 1
                        }
                    }
                    at = 0
                    for q to ne_here {
                        if ew[q] != SEQUENCE_WEIGHT and ((end == 0 and efrom[q] == i) or (end == 1 and eto[q] == i)) {
                            at += 1
                            off = (at / (count + 1) - 0.5) * PORT_SPREAD * kw[i]
                            if end == 0 {
                                sp[q] = off
                            }
                            else {
                                tp[q] = off
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            inp0 = layout_input(kw, kh, efrom, eto, INNER_NODE_GAP, INNER_RANK_GAP)
            inp = LayoutInput { eback: eback, eweight: ew, elen: zeros(ne_here) + 2, sport: sp, tport: tp, ..inp0 }
            for q to len(efrom) {
                if len(evars[q]) > 0 {
                    lab = names_label(evars[q])
                    inp.label_w[q] = text_w(lab, FONT_SMALL, 1)
                    inp.label_h[q] = FONT_SMALL + LINE_GAP
                }
            }
            L = layered(inp)
            for i to nk {
                relx[kids[i]] = L.x[i]
                rely[kids[i]] = L.y[i]
            }
            inner_w = max(L.width, max(hw[d], fw[d]))
            bw[d] = inner_w + 2 * PAD
            bh[d] = hh[d] + L.height + PAD + fh[d]
            cox[d] = PAD + (inner_w - L.width) / 2
            coy[d] = hh[d]
            for q to len(efrom) {
                r_owner = append(r_owner, d)
                r_start = append(r_start, len(r_x))
                r_x = extend(r_x, L.route_x[L.route_start[q]:L.route_start[q + 1]])
                r_y = extend(r_y, L.route_y[L.route_start[q]:L.route_start[q + 1]])
                r_style = append(r_style, estyle[q])
                r_id = append(r_id, eid[q])
                lab = ""
                if len(evars[q]) > 0 {
                    lab = names_label(evars[q])
                }
                r_label = append(r_label, lab)
                r_lx = append(r_lx, L.label_x[q])
                r_ly = append(r_ly, L.label_y[q])
            }
        }
    }
    nr = len(r_owner)
    r_start = append(r_start, len(r_x))

    # ---- every node's place inside its def's box (top-left corners)
    tlx = zeros(m)
    tly = zeros(m)
    for level from 1 to maxdepth + 1 {
        for d to m {
            if depth[d] == level {
                p = par[d]
                tlx[d] = tlx[p] + cox[p] + relx[d] - bw[d] / 2
                tly[d] = tly[p] + coy[p] + rely[d] - bh[d] / 2
            }
        }
    }

    # ---- the defs, left to right: callers before callees
    defs = []
    for d to m {
        if depth[d] == 0 {
            defs = append(defs, d)
        }
    }
    nd = len(defs)
    dlocal = zeros(m) - 1
    for i to nd {
        dlocal[defs[i]] = i
    }
    # one arrow per caller and callee: from the first step that makes the
    # call (or the def's header), with the most times any of them ran
    cfrom = []
    cto = []
    cport = []
    cstep = []
    csrc = []
    ccount = []
    cid = split("")
    cstyle = split("")
    cxlab = split("")
    # the ranks each call spans: 2 for one whose label needs a rank of its own
    celen = []
    for e to len(g.edge_kinds) {
        if g.edge_kinds[e] != "call" {
            continue
        }
        src = dmap[g.edge_from[e]]
        callee = dmap[g.edge_to[e]]
        if src < 0 or callee < 0 {
            continue
        }
        caller = dmap[g.owners[g.edge_from[e]]]
        # an open multi-path takes the call from its host to a member through its fork
        through_fork = false
        for k to len(mp.ids) {
            if mp.open[k] == 1 and mp.hosts[k] == gi[caller] and g.labels[gi[callee]] in split(mp.members[k]) {
                through_fork = true
            }
        }
        if through_fork {
            continue
        }
        a = dlocal[caller]
        b = dlocal[callee]
        dup = -1
        for q to len(cfrom) {
            if cfrom[q] == a and cto[q] == b {
                dup = q
            }
        }
        if dup >= 0 {
            ccount[dup] = max(ccount[dup], view.counts[e])
            continue
        }
        cfrom = append(cfrom, a)
        cto = append(cto, b)
        ccount = append(ccount, view.counts[e])
        csrc = append(csrc, src)
        cid = append(cid, "call:" + g.ids[gi[src]] + "->" + g.ids[gi[callee]])
        cstyle = append(cstyle, "ink")
        cxlab = append(cxlab, "")
        celen = append(celen, 1)
        if src == caller {
            # a call outside every step leaves at the def's header
            cport = append(cport, head_h[caller] / 2 - bh[caller] / 2)
            cstep = append(cstep, -1)
        }
        else {
            cport = append(cport, tly[src] + bh[src] / 2 - bh[caller] / 2)
            cstep = append(cstep, src)
        }
    }
    # ---- the multi-paths: boxes of their own among the defs' boxes
    oids = split("")
    for i to nd {
        oids = append(oids, g.ids[gi[defs[i]]])
    }
    # per synthetic box: its id, its kind (`closed`, `fork`, `join`, `member`),
    # its lines of text and its style
    syn_d = []
    syn_id = split("")
    syn_kind = split("")
    syn_l1 = split("")
    syn_l2 = split("")
    syn_l3 = split("")
    syn_l4 = split("")
    syn_style = split("")
    for k to len(mp.ids) {
        if mp.hosts[k] < 0 {
            continue
        }
        h = dmap[mp.hosts[k]]
        if h < 0 or depth[h] != 0 {
            continue
        }
        hs = -1
        if mp.host_steps[k] >= 0 and dmap[mp.host_steps[k]] >= 0 {
            hs = dmap[mp.host_steps[k]]
        }
        key = "mp:" + mp.ids[k] + "@" + g.ids[mp.hosts[k]]
        ms = split(mp.members[k])
        nm = len(ms)
        kinds = split("")
        ids = split("")
        l1 = split("")
        l2 = split("")
        l3 = split("")
        l4 = split("")
        sty = split("")
        if mp.open[k] == 0 {
            kinds = ["closed"]
            ids = [key]
            l1 = [clean(fit(mp.ids[k] + " · multi-path ×" + grouped(nm), HEADER_MAX_W, FONT_NORMAL, 1))]
            l2 = [clean(fit(mp.titles[k], HEADER_MAX_W, FONT_SMALL, 0))]
            l3 = [clean(fit("agree " + mp.contracts[k], HEADER_MAX_W, FONT_SMALL, 0))]
            l4 = [clean(fit(mp.notes[k], HEADER_MAX_W, FONT_SMALL, 0))]
            sty = ["s3 tint"]
        }
        else {
            kinds = ["fork"]
            ids = [key + "/fork"]
            l1 = [clean(mp.ids[k] + " ×" + grouped(nm))]
            l2 = [""]
            l3 = [""]
            l4 = [""]
            sty = ["s3 tint diamond"]
            for mm in ms {
                j = node_index(g, mm)
                if j >= 0 and dmap[j] >= 0 and depth[dmap[j]] == 0 {
                    continue
                }
                kinds = append(kinds, "member")
                ids = append(ids, key + "/m:" + mm)
                l1 = append(l1, clean(mm))
                role = "cross-check"
                style = "muted plain dash"
                if mm == mp.defaults[k] {
                    role = "default"
                    style = "s1 tint"
                }
                if mm in split(mp.ran[k]) {
                    role = role + ", ran"
                }
                l2 = append(l2, role)
                l3 = append(l3, "")
                l4 = append(l4, "")
                sty = append(sty, style)
            }
            kinds = append(kinds, "join")
            ids = append(ids, key + "/join")
            l1 = append(l1, "agree")
            l2 = append(l2, clean(fit(mp.contracts[k], 120, FONT_SMALL, 0)))
            l3 = append(l3, "")
            l4 = append(l4, "")
            sty = append(sty, "s3 tint diamond")
        }
        # sizes, and a place among the defs' boxes
        first = len(bw)
        for i to len(kinds) {
            w1 = text_w(l1[i], FONT_NORMAL, 1)
            if kinds[i] == "fork" or kinds[i] == "join" {
                w1 = max(text_w(l1[i], FONT_SMALL, 1), text_w(l2[i], FONT_SMALL, 0))
                lines = 1
                if len(l2[i]) > 0 {
                    lines = 2
                }
                bw = append(bw, diamond_w(w1))
                bh = append(bh, diamond_h(lines))
                head_h = append(head_h, diamond_h(lines))
            }
            else {
                w1 = max(w1, max(text_w(l2[i], FONT_SMALL, 0), max(text_w(l3[i], FONT_SMALL, 0), text_w(l4[i], FONT_SMALL, 0))))
                below = 0
                for txt in [l2[i], l3[i], l4[i]] {
                    if len(txt) > 0 {
                        below += 1
                    }
                }
                bw = append(bw, max(w1 + 2 * PAD, STEP_MIN_W))
                bh = append(bh, FONT_NORMAL + 2 * PAD + below * (FONT_SMALL + LINE_GAP))
                head_h = append(head_h, FONT_NORMAL + 2 * PAD)
            }
            dlocal = append(dlocal, len(defs))
            defs = append(defs, len(bw) - 1)
            oids = append(oids, ids[i])
            syn_d = append(syn_d, len(bw) - 1)
            syn_id = append(syn_id, ids[i])
            syn_kind = append(syn_kind, kinds[i])
            syn_l1 = append(syn_l1, l1[i])
            syn_l2 = append(syn_l2, l2[i])
            syn_l3 = append(syn_l3, l3[i])
            syn_l4 = append(syn_l4, l4[i])
            syn_style = append(syn_style, sty[i])
        }
        # the call into the stage: from the step that makes it, or the host's header
        into = dlocal[first]
        cfrom = append(cfrom, dlocal[h])
        cto = append(cto, into)
        ccount = append(ccount, 0)
        csrc = append(csrc, h)
        if hs >= 0 {
            cport = append(cport, tly[hs] + bh[hs] / 2 - bh[h] / 2)
            cstep = append(cstep, hs)
            csrc[len(csrc) - 1] = hs
        }
        else {
            cport = append(cport, head_h[h] / 2 - bh[h] / 2)
            cstep = append(cstep, -1)
        }
        cid = append(cid, key + "/in")
        cstyle = append(cstyle, "ink")
        inlab = ""
        if mp.open[k] == 1 {
            inlab = clean(fit(mp.titles[k], 2 * STEP_MAX_W, FONT_SMALL, 1))
        }
        cxlab = append(cxlab, inlab)
        if len(inlab) > 0 {
            celen = append(celen, 2)
        }
        else {
            celen = append(celen, 1)
        }
        if mp.open[k] == 1 {
            fk = dlocal[first]
            jn = dlocal[len(bw) - 1]
            for mm in ms {
                # the member's box: a drawn def, or its own
                j = node_index(g, mm)
                target = -1
                if j >= 0 and dmap[j] >= 0 and depth[dmap[j]] == 0 {
                    target = dlocal[dmap[j]]
                }
                else {
                    target = dlocal[first + index(syn_id[len(syn_id) - (len(bw) - first):], key + "/m:" + mm)]
                }
                style = "muted dash"
                if mm == mp.defaults[k] {
                    style = "ink thick"
                }
                for leg to 2 {
                    a = fk
                    b = target
                    lid = key + "/to:" + mm
                    if leg == 1 {
                        a = target
                        b = jn
                        lid = key + "/from:" + mm
                    }
                    cfrom = append(cfrom, a)
                    cto = append(cto, b)
                    ccount = append(ccount, 0)
                    csrc = append(csrc, -1)
                    cstep = append(cstep, -1)
                    src_d = defs[a]
                    cport = append(cport, head_h[src_d] / 2 - bh[src_d] / 2)
                    cid = append(cid, lid)
                    cstyle = append(cstyle, style)
                    cxlab = append(cxlab, "")
                    celen = append(celen, 1)
                }
            }
        }
    }
    nd = len(defs)
    nc = len(cfrom)
    clab = []
    for q to nc {
        lab = ""
        if ccount[q] > 1 {
            lab = "×" + grouped(ccount[q])
        }
        if len(cxlab[q]) > 0 {
            lab = cxlab[q]
        }
        clab = append(clab, lab)
    }
    # top to bottom, each call from a step runs down its own lane on the right
    # of its def's box, so it does not cross the box's other steps
    clane = zeros(nc)
    nlanes = zeros(nd)
    for q to nc {
        if cstep[q] >= 0 {
            clane[q] = nlanes[cfrom[q]]
            nlanes[cfrom[q]] += 1
        }
    }
    down = view.dir == 2
    O = layered(outer_input(oids, view, defs, bw, bh, head_h, cfrom, cto, cport, cstep, clab, celen, clane, nlanes, down))
    # a drawing far wider than tall reads better top to bottom: callers above
    # callees, a call leaving down the right side of its caller's box
    if view.dir == 0 and O.height > WIDE_RATIO * O.width {
        down = true
        O = layered(outer_input(oids, view, defs, bw, bh, head_h, cfrom, cto, cport, cstep, clab, celen, clane, nlanes, true))
    }
    lw = zeros(nd)
    if down {
        lw = nlanes * LANE_GAP
    }
    ax = zeros(len(bw))
    ay = zeros(len(bw))
    for i to nd {
        d = defs[i]
        if down {
            ax[d] = O.x[i] - (bw[d] + lw[i]) / 2
            ay[d] = LEGEND_H + O.y[i] - bh[d] / 2
        }
        else {
            ax[d] = O.y[i] - bw[d] / 2
            ay[d] = LEGEND_H + O.x[i] - bh[d] / 2
        }
    }
    for level from 1 to maxdepth + 1 {
        for d to m {
            if depth[d] == level {
                root = d
                while par[root] >= 0 {
                    root = par[root]
                }
                ax[d] = ax[root] + tlx[d]
                ay[d] = ay[root] + tly[d]
            }
        }
    }
    width = max(O.height, 1)
    height = LEGEND_H + max(O.width, 1)
    way = "across"
    if down {
        width = max(O.width, 1)
        height = LEGEND_H + max(O.height, 1)
        way = "down"
    }
    # the legend's line, when there are multi-paths, is as wide as the drawing at least
    if len(syn_d) > 0 {
        legend_w = 0
        for lt in ["calls", "values a step hands on", "values for the next pass", "a multi-path: several implementations of one intent, held to agree"] {
            legend_w += 26 + PAD + text_w(lt, FONT_SMALL, 0) + 2 * PAD
        }
        width = max(width, legend_w)
    }

    # ---- the records: boxes outside in, then arrows, then text
    figure(title, way, "", 0, width, -height, 0, "diagram")
    for level from 0 to maxdepth + 1 {
        for d to m {
            if depth[d] != level {
                continue
            }
            k = gi[d]
            style = "muted plain"
            if g.kinds[k] == "def" {
                style = "s1 tint"
            }
            else if g.kinds[k] == "loop" {
                style = "s2 clear dash"
            }
            else if nkids[d] > 0 {
                style = "muted tint"
            }
            box(g.ids[k], style, ax[d], -(ay[d] + bh[d]), ax[d] + bw[d], -ay[d])
        }
    }
    # the multi-paths' boxes: a closed stage, a fork, a member, a join
    for i to len(syn_d) {
        d = syn_d[i]
        box(syn_id[i], syn_style[i], ax[d], -(ay[d] + bh[d]), ax[d] + bw[d], -ay[d])
    }
    # calls between defs: from the calling step's right side to the callee's header
    for q to nc {
        lo = O.route_start[q]
        hi = O.route_start[q + 1]
        xs = []
        ys = []
        if cstep[q] >= 0 {
            s = cstep[q]
            xs = append(xs, ax[s] + bw[s])
            ys = append(ys, -(ay[s] + bh[s] / 2))
            if down {
                xs = append(xs, O.route_x[lo])
                ys = append(ys, -(ay[s] + bh[s] / 2))
            }
        }
        for i from lo to hi {
            if down {
                xs = append(xs, O.route_x[i])
                ys = append(ys, -(LEGEND_H + O.route_y[i]))
            }
            else {
                xs = append(xs, O.route_y[i])
                ys = append(ys, -(LEGEND_H + O.route_x[i]))
            }
        }
        # straight pieces: a curve through the corners of a long route swings
        # wide of them, across the boxes beside it
        id = cid[q]
        arrow(id, cstyle[q], xs, ys)
        if len(clab[q]) > 0 {
            if down {
                note(id + "#count", clab[q], "muted small mono", O.label_x[q], -(LEGEND_H + O.label_y[q]))
            }
            else {
                note(id + "#count", clab[q], "muted small mono", O.label_y[q], -(LEGEND_H + O.label_x[q]))
            }
        }
    }
    # values and order inside boxes
    for q to nr {
        d = r_owner[q]
        ox = ax[d] + cox[d]
        oy = ay[d] + coy[d]
        xs = r_x[r_start[q]:r_start[q + 1]] + ox
        ys = -(r_y[r_start[q]:r_start[q + 1]] + oy)
        arrow(r_id[q], r_style[q], xs, ys)
        if len(r_label[q]) > 0 {
            color = "s5"
            if startswith(r_style[q], "s2") {
                color = "s2"
            }
            note(r_id[q] + "#vars", r_label[q], color + " small mono", ox + r_lx[q], -(oy + r_ly[q]))
        }
    }
    for d to m {
        k = gi[d]
        x0 = ax[d] + PAD
        y0 = ay[d] + PAD
        if g.kinds[k] == "def" {
            note(g.ids[k] + "#head", head[d], "ink left top mono bold", x0, -y0)
            if len(marks[d]) > 0 {
                which = "#more"
                if marks[d] == "−" {
                    which = "#less"
                }
                note(g.ids[k] + which, marks[d], "s1 right top mono bold small", ax[d] + bw[d] - PAD, -(y0 + (FONT_NORMAL - FONT_SMALL) / 2))
            }
        }
        else if g.kinds[k] == "loop" {
            note(g.ids[k] + "#head", head[d], "s2 left top mono small", x0, -y0)
        }
        else {
            note(g.ids[k] + "#head", head[d], "ink left top mono bold", x0, -y0)
            below = y0 + FONT_NORMAL + LINE_GAP
            if len(sub[d]) > 0 {
                note(g.ids[k] + "#text", sub[d], "muted left top small", x0, -below)
                below += FONT_SMALL + LINE_GAP
            }
            if len(ins[d]) > 0 {
                note(g.ids[k] + "#reads", ins[d], "s5 left top small mono", x0, -below)
            }
        }
        if len(foot[d]) > 0 {
            note(g.ids[k] + "#foot", foot[d], "muted left bottom small", x0, -(ay[d] + bh[d] - PAD / 2))
        }
    }
    for i to len(syn_d) {
        d = syn_d[i]
        sk = syn_kind[i]
        if sk == "fork" or sk == "join" {
            cx = ax[d] + bw[d] / 2
            if len(syn_l2[i]) > 0 {
                note(syn_id[i] + "#head", syn_l1[i], "s3 small mono bold", cx, -(ay[d] + bh[d] / 2 - (FONT_SMALL + LINE_GAP) / 2))
                note(syn_id[i] + "#text", syn_l2[i], "muted small", cx, -(ay[d] + bh[d] / 2 + (FONT_SMALL + LINE_GAP) / 2))
            }
            else {
                note(syn_id[i] + "#head", syn_l1[i], "s3 small mono bold", cx, -(ay[d] + bh[d] / 2))
            }
            continue
        }
        x0 = ax[d] + PAD
        y0 = ay[d] + PAD
        note(syn_id[i] + "#head", syn_l1[i], "ink left top mono bold", x0, -y0)
        below = y0 + FONT_NORMAL + LINE_GAP
        parts = ["#text", "#contract", "#note"]
        texts = [syn_l2[i], syn_l3[i], syn_l4[i]]
        for t to 3 {
            if len(texts[t]) > 0 {
                note(syn_id[i] + parts[t], texts[t], "muted left top small", x0, -below)
                below += FONT_SMALL + LINE_GAP
            }
        }
    }
    # the legend, above
    lx = 0
    ly = -LEGEND_H / 2
    key_w = 26
    arrow("legend:call", "ink", [lx, lx + key_w], [ly, ly])
    note("legend:call#text", "calls", "muted left small", lx + key_w + PAD / 2, ly)
    lx += key_w + PAD + text_w("calls", FONT_SMALL, 0) + 2 * PAD
    arrow("legend:data", "s5", [lx, lx + key_w], [ly, ly])
    note("legend:data#text", "values a step hands on", "muted left small", lx + key_w + PAD / 2, ly)
    lx += key_w + PAD + text_w("values a step hands on", FONT_SMALL, 0) + 2 * PAD
    arrow("legend:next", "s2 dash", [lx, lx + key_w], [ly, ly])
    note("legend:next#text", "values for the next pass", "muted left small", lx + key_w + PAD / 2, ly)
    if len(syn_d) > 0 {
        lx += key_w + PAD + text_w("values for the next pass", FONT_SMALL, 0) + 2 * PAD
        # a small diamond, drawn as a closed line
        dh = FONT_SMALL / 2
        arrow("legend:multipath", "s3 nohead", [lx, lx + dh, lx + 2 * dh, lx + dh, lx], [ly, ly + dh, ly, ly - dh, ly])
        note("legend:multipath#text", "a multi-path: several implementations of one intent, held to agree", "muted left small", lx + 2 * dh + PAD / 2, ly)
    }
    return nd
}

test "a program with steps: the defs with steps are drawn, with their steps" {
    g = graph_of_self()
    # this module has no steps: every def the run reaches, which is none
    assert_true(sum(chosen_defs(g)) == 1)
    assert_true(fit("abcdefghij", 5 * FONT_SMALL * MONO_EM, FONT_SMALL, 1) == "abcd…")
    assert_true(names_label("D F") == "D, F")
    assert_true(clean("a ; b\nc") == "a; b c")
    assert_true(grouped(47270) == "47,270" and grouped(3) == "3" and grouped(1234567) == "1,234,567" and grouped(100) == "100")
}

